aland ahead by six, and her roughly 20-to-1 fundraising advantage reinforces New Mexico's Democratic lean in an open seat. Raters across the spectrum call the race Likely or Solid D, and prediction markets price her near 95 percent, supporting a mid-to-high single-digit expected margin.", "watch": "A nationalized late environment or Hull breaking through on his income-tax repeal message while Haaland skips debates could narrow the race.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Michelle Lujan Grisham (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Mexico's governorship is open this year as Michelle Lujan Grisham terms out, with Democrat Deb Haaland and Republican Gregg Hull on the ballot. The state leans Democratic by about four points, though the open seat removes the usual incumbent cushion.\n\nHaaland has led by about six points in the most recent independent polls and holds an overwhelming fundraising edge, roughly $11 million raised against under $500,000 for Hull. Rating outlets mostly call the race Likely or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets price her chances near 95 percent. Hull's income-tax repeal pitch and a standoff over debates leave some room for movement, but the evidence points to a clear Haaland advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 10.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9605, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.948, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9415, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9502, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9552, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9463, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9606, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9549, "margin": 10.